      "title": "Continental Drift Theory | Evidence | Distribution of Ocean and Continents | 11th Geography | NCERT",
      "description": "Continental Drift Theory | Evidence | Distribution of Ocean and Continents | 11th Geography | NCERT\n\n📲 Connect with Final Attempt\n🎯Telegram: https://t.me/finalattemptofficial\n🎯Instagram: https://instagram.com/finalattempt_official\n🎯YouTube: https://youtube.com/@FinalAttemptOfficial\n🎯Website: https://finalattemptias.com\n\nIn this lecture, we cover Continental Drift Theory from NCERT Class 11 Geography (Chapter 4 – Distribution of Oceans and Continents) in a simple, conceptual, and exam-oriented manner.\n\nThis video explains Alfred Wegener's Continental Drift Theory, the concept of Pangaea, Panthalassa, Laurasia, Gondwanaland, and the evidence supporting continental drift. It is highly useful for BPSC, UPSC, State PCS, CUET, UGC NET, SSC, Teaching Exams, and all Geography learners.\n\n📚 Topics Covered:\n✔️ Continental Drift Theory\n✔️ Alfred Wegener\n✔️ Pangaea (Supercontinent)\n✔️ Panthalassa\n✔️ Laurasia\n✔️ Gondwanaland\n✔️ Drift of Continents\n✔️ Evidence of Continental Drift\n✔️ Fossil Evidence\n✔️ Geological Evidence\n✔️ Climatic Evidence\n✔️ Limitations of Wegener's Theory\n✔️ NCERT Class 11 Geography Chapter 4\n✔️ Distribution of Oceans and Continents\n\n🎯 Useful For:\n• BPSC Prelims & Mains\n• UPSC CSE\n• State PCS\n• CUET\n• UGC NET Geography\n• SSC & Other Competitive Exams\n• Class 11 NCERT Geography Students\n\n📖 NCERT Chapter:\nClass 11 Geography – Chapter 4\nDistribution of Oceans and Continents\n\n🔔 Subscribe to Final Attempt for high-quality Geography lectures, NCERT Series, Bihar Special Content, Current Affairs, and complete BPSC & UPSC preparation.\n\n#ContinentalDriftTheory #AlfredWegener #Pangea #Panthalassa #Gondwanaland #Laurasia #DistributionOfOceansAndContinents #NCERTGeography #Class11Geography #Geography #PhysicalGeography #Geomorphology #EarthScience #NCERT #UPSC #UPSCGeography #BPSC #BPSC2026 #StatePCS #CompetitiveExams #GeographyLecture #FinalAttempt",
